2. Definitions

   "Licensed Methods" means the data synchronization and prioritization
   methods used in EveSynapse, including:

     (a) building pages and page sections only from locally stored data,
         while separate background processes retrieve data from
         rate-limited external services;

     (b) recording data that a page could not show when it was built, and
         ordering its retrieval ahead of other work because a user is
         viewing that page;

     (c) ordering retrieval by how close data is to a user, including data
         the user is viewing, data indicated by the user's search input
         while the user is typing, data referenced by the user's own
         records, and data one or more relationships removed from those
         records, ranked by distance and recency; and

     (d) spending all such retrieval from a shared, bounded budget that
         slows or stops when the external service signals a rate or error
         limit.

